# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# /storm was a placeholder that never described an event: its copy read "when a
# storm event is active ... Kahu Ola will surface context here", under a title
# of "Active Storm Tracker". Nothing on the site linked to it, so the only way
# in was organic search — which is exactly the arrival that matters, because a
# resident searching mid-event landed on a page that read as "nothing is
# happening" while a real watch was posted. The live map is what that reader
# wanted, and the page's own text already said so.
#
# Cloudflare Pages already 308s /storm.html -> /storm, so that request now
# chains 308 -> 301 and still ends at the live map. The explicit .html rule is
# kept so the destination does not depend on that built-in behaviour.
/storm       /live-map  301
/storm.html  /live-map  301

# Invariant 2. /Maui and the statewide wireframe served hazard STATES that were
# typed into the HTML and fetched from nothing: "Flood Watch is in effect for
# Maui County", "AQI 67 — Moderate", "Storm Watch · Active", "Updated just now".
# The wireframe had not been touched since 2026-03-11. Both were indexable, and
# a resident searching "maui flood watch" could land on an NWS product claim
# that no feed ever issued. Deleted; these send that traffic to the live map,
# which answers the same question from real data.
#
# Measured on the live host 2026-09-24, BEFORE deletion:
#   /Maui                                              200  the fabricated page
#   /Maui.html                                         308 -> /Maui
#   /Hawai%CA%BBi%20statewide%20page%20wireframe       200  the fabricated page
#   /Hawai...wireframe.html                            308 -> extensionless form
#   /maui  /maui.html  /hawaii-statewide.html          200  index.html fallback
# Pages matches file paths case-SENSITIVELY and falls back to index.html with
# 200 for anything unmatched, so the lowercase and hyphenated spellings never
# served the fabricated content. They are listed anyway: after deletion they
# would otherwise fall through to that silent 200 homepage, and a stale link or
# bookmark is better answered by the live map than by a page that looks like it
# worked. The percent-encoded source is the only writable form — _redirects is
# whitespace-delimited, so the literal space cannot be expressed.
/Maui.html                                        /live-map  301
/Maui                                             /live-map  301
/maui.html                                        /live-map  301
/maui                                             /live-map  301
/hawaii-statewide.html                            /live-map  301
/Hawai%CA%BBi%20statewide%20page%20wireframe.html /live-map  301
/Hawai%CA%BBi%20statewide%20page%20wireframe      /live-map  301
